config BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_PYTHON_EMPY
	bool "host python-empy"
	help
	  Empy is a system for embedding Python expressions and statements
	  in template text; it takes an Empy source file, processes it, and
	  produces output.

	  This is accomplished via expansions, which are special signals to
	  the Empy system and are set off by a special prefix (by default
	  the at sign, '@'). Empy can expand arbitrary Python expressions
	  and statements in this way, as well as a variety of special
	  forms. Text that does not contain special forms is left
	  undisturbed.

	  https://github.com/alecthomas/empy

	  This is the host version.
